From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: escalate an L1 SER that never reaches
 RESET_DONE

If the firmware never signals RESET_DONE, the L1 path skipped the DMA
reset and token reclaim, waited another 30 s for NORMAL_STATE, then
restarted DMA on top of rings that were never reset, with tokens
possibly leaking until tx stayed blocked.

Queue a full recovery instead of resuming.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index 00abadfe..e7be7ccd 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1605,6 +1605,13 @@ void mt7915_mac_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 		mt76_wr(dev, MT_MCU_INT_EVENT, MT_MCU_INT_EVENT_DMA_INIT);
 		mt7915_wait_reset_state(dev, MT_MCU_CMD_RECOVERY_DONE);
+	} else if (!mt7915_reset_aborted(dev)) {
+		/* No RESET_DONE: the rings were not reset and the tokens not
+		 * reclaimed, don't resume on top of them.
+		 */
+		dev->recovery.restart = true;
+		queue_work(dev->mt76.wq, &dev->reset_work);
+		goto out_aborted;
 	}
 
 	if (mt7915_reset_aborted(dev))
